## Motivation With `--tool-call-parser deepseekv3` and `tools` in the request, a streamed answer loses every ``` in its normal content, while the same answer without streaming keeps them. Code blocks in DeepSeek-V3, V3-0324 and R1-0528 answers arrive at the client as bare text: `json
{...}
` instead of a fenced block. Clients that send tools and stream, as most coding agents do, hit this on every answer that contains code. `--tool-call-parser auto` also picks `deepseekv3` for these templates. `DeepSeekV3Detector.parse_streaming_increment` strips `"```"` from any text that has no tool-call marker (`deepseekv3_detector.py:104`). `detect_and_parse` (non-streaming) does not strip it, and `DeepSeekV31Detector` leaves fences alone in the same branch. Repro (one token per delta, the default `--stream-interval 1`): ``` non-stream: 'Here is an example:
```json
{"a": 1, "b": [2]}
```
Done.' stream : 'Here is an example:
json
{"a": 1, "b": [2]}

Done.' ``` ## Modifications - `deepseekv3_detector.py`: stop removing `"```"` from normal text in `parse_streaming_increment`. The EOS and `<｜tool▁call▁end｜>` tokens are still removed. - Why the strip existed: `"```"` was added in #5592, when the partial call regex did not require the closing fence and the buffer was cleared before the fence arrived. #7562 made the regex require the closing fence, so since then the strip has only removed fences from user answers. - The fences around tool-call arguments never reach this branch: the call regex needs the closing fence before it matches, and the completed call is then cut from the buffer

